# Illegal: agreeing on a type is not enough. `+` on two strings emits
# `add ptr`, which clang will not assemble - so without this check the compiler
# produces a file that is not a program and reports nothing.
#
# `==` on two strings is refused for a reason rather than for a gap: a string is
# a borrowed view, so it would compare addresses. std/core/text.yoop:equals is
# the comparison that was meant.
#
# All five are reported: one bad operator should not hide the next.
24:33: operator "+" cannot be applied to string and string
25:30: operator "==" cannot be applied to string and string
29:32: operator "+" cannot be applied to Point and Point
33:37: operator "<" cannot be applied to bool and bool
37:29: operator "<" cannot be applied to Shape and Shape
